{"type":"standard","title":"Sanford Bishop","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Sanford Bishop</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q983428","titles":{"canonical":"Sanford_Bishop","normalized":"Sanford Bishop","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Sanford Bishop</span></span>"},"pageid":411731,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Official_photo_of_Sen._Sanford_Bishop.jpg/330px-Official_photo_of_Sen._Sanford_Bishop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":400},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Official_photo_of_Sen._Sanford_Bishop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1525,"height":1849},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1363278609","tid":"6ad35d72-7b51-11f1-aa5e-e0630ea35701","timestamp":"2026-07-09T04:48:24Z","description":"American politician (born 1947)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanford_Bishop","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanford_Bishop?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanford_Bishop?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Sanford_Bishop"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanford_Bishop","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Sanford_Bishop","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanford_Bishop?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Sanford_Bishop"}},"extract":"Sanford Dixon Bishop Jr. is an American lawyer and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Georgia's 2nd congressional district since 1993. He became the dean of Georgia's congressional delegation after the death of John Lewis. A member of the Blue Dog Coalition, he belongs to the moderate faction of the Democratic Party. His district is in southwestern Georgia and includes Albany, Thomasville, and most of Columbus and Macon.","extract_html":"<p><b>Sanford Dixon Bishop Jr.</b> is an American lawyer and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Georgia's 2nd congressional district since 1993. He became the dean of Georgia's congressional delegation after the death of John Lewis. A member of the Blue Dog Coalition, he belongs to the moderate faction of the Democratic Party. His district is in southwestern Georgia and includes Albany, Thomasville, and most of Columbus and Macon.</p>"}